46:   So the two escapes are NOT an artifact of the 14-row table-1 instrument.  The five rows added
47:   between 14 and 19 -- a position row (`ycrcb x4y1', vertex 4,1) and the RE-window priming rows --
48:   move the x/y and window axes, and every one of them still drives its DECLINED type at
49:   MODE_YCRCB 0x12f0 or MODE_RESERVED 0x1250, i.e. BUFDEPTH_32 on LIN_A.  The width axis and the
50:   tiled axis are untouched by the repair, so both cells stay empty and both mutants stay invisible.
