2281:`M6_cond` is the canonical clause-(d) form �?" guard kept, repair conditioned on a field the guarded
2282:body reads:
2283:
2284:```c
2285:	case DE_MODE_TYPE_RGB:
2286:		if (bufdepth == 4)  *color = (buf[0]<<24)+(buf[1]<<16)+(buf[2]<<8);   /* the fix */
2287:		else                *color = (buf[1]<<24)+(buf[2]<<16)+(buf[3]<<8);   /* the defect */
2288:```
2289:
2290:**Every session in the 6-row detector used `BUFDEPTH_32`, so `bufdepth` was 4 in all of them and the
2291:mutant's fix branch was the only one the detector ever executed.** It proved the fix works exactly
2292:where I measured it and said nothing whatever about anywhere else. `bufdepth` is not an exotic
2293:choice: it is read by the guarded body (it is `memory_rw`'s transfer length) and comes from **bits
2294:8-9 of the same mode word** whose bits 4-7 the guard reads. The DEPENDS-ON closure enumerates it
2295:first, not last.
