OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md
18043:`fatal()` -- `dst_tlb` values 3, 6 and 7 come straight from a guest `MTE_MODE` write (the DST_BUF field),
18044:one message per transfer, unbounded. A READING by the Opus seat during the `sgimtelabelcells` table, not a
18045:measurement. Not a host kill (`fatal()` returns); a `floodclass` member. The fix shape is settled by the
18046:file's own ten-bit `SGIRE_W_*` latch enum and its "own bit, never shared" precedent; the measurement is one
18047:session in the shape `fill_at(A, RE_TLB_A, 3 << 2)` from the repaired `regress/sgi_mte_fill_probe.py`.
18048:
18049:### `sgiretlbshiftub` (med) -- filed 2026-09-10
18050:
18051:`dev_sgi_re.c` `horrible_getputpixel()`, anchor `tileptr = d->re_tlb_a[tile_nr] << 16`: the three TLB
18052:arrays are `uint16_t`, which promotes to `int`, so this is a SIGNED left shift and any entry with bit 15
18053:set overflows `INT_MAX` -- undefined behaviour. **It is the only path that works**: two lines below, the
18054:model accepts a tile pointer only `if (tileptr & 0x80000000)`, and bit 31 can only come from bit 15 of
18055:the `uint16_t`, so every ACCEPTED pointer overflows and every non-overflowing one is REJECTED. The three
18056:arrays are written by ordinary guest register writes, so the guest picks the value. `re_linear_a` is
18057:`uint32_t` and is NOT affected (unsigned wrap, defined). Fix: three casts to `uint32_t`. Found by the
18058:codex seat under the found-something-else licence while answering a `#519` test-coverage question
18059:(`regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/codex_coverage_20260910.txt`); verified by reading before filing.
18060:Witness OWED as an ATTEMPT: a `-fsanitize=undefined` build in `build-asan/` is the first thing to try,
18061:since a rung-3 guest witness may be impossible for UB that behaves as intended on every compiler here.
